Coding Guidelines (2025-Ready)
PHP / WordPress

Min PHP: 8.1

Use scalar and return type hints wherever reasonable.

Avoid deprecated functions; check the WP dev reference for replacements.

Use wp_enqueue_script() / wp_enqueue_style() properly.

Never access $_GET, $_POST, $_REQUEST, $_SERVER without sanitization.

Security

Escape any output to HTML using:

esc_html(), esc_attr(), esc_url(), wp_kses(), etc.

Sanitize inputs on save:

sanitize_text_field(), sanitize_key(), absint(), floatval(), etc.

Use nonces for any form/action:

wp_nonce_field(), check_admin_referer()

Always check capabilities:

current_user_can('manage_options') for settings page.

Performance

Only run optimization logic if plugin is enabled.

Avoid expensive DB queries on each page load.

Use options and transients instead of custom tables unless needed.

Keep admin scripts/styles small and only load on plugin pages.

i18n

Wrap all user-visible strings:

__('Text', 'auto-web-vitals-optimizer')

esc_html_e('Text', 'auto-web-vitals-optimizer')

Generate .pot file in languages/.

Code Style

Follow PSR-12 as much as feasible with WordPress.

4 spaces indentation, no tabs.

Class names: StudlyCaps.

Namespaces: AutoWebVitals\{Layer}.

Keep file/class mapping consistent for the autoloader.

Prefix everything (awvo_ or AutoWebVitals namespace) to avoid conflicts.